diff --git a/docs/sphinx/source/adding_data.rst b/docs/sphinx/source/adding_data.rst
index 09c713e..a52d892 100644
--- a/docs/sphinx/source/adding_data.rst
+++ b/docs/sphinx/source/adding_data.rst
@@ -129,6 +129,16 @@ You can add fixes to your dataset by following examples in the ``aqua/core/confi
     (``aqua.core.intake_drivers.xarray``), keeping the same catalog syntax as
     the former intake-xarray ones.
 
+Options that control the xarray open call (``engine``, ``chunks``, ``decode_times``, ...)
+can be set either in ``args.xarray_kwargs`` or directly in ``args``.
+When the same option is given in both, the explicit one wins: source and ``Reader``
+kwargs override the catalog ``xarray_kwargs``, which override the driver defaults.
+A mapping such as ``chunks`` is replaced as a whole rather than merged key by key, and
+an explicit ``chunks: null`` is kept, so it bypasses dask.
+The options the source reads with (driver defaults, catalog ``xarray_kwargs`` and the
+explicit ones) are exposed through its ``xarray_kwargs`` attribute, which the backend
+uses again when reading, so an overridden catalog value cannot come back.
+
 .. _stac-based-sources:
 
 STAC-based sources
